Delcan wrote:
> Candles don't get enough respect.  All you can really use them for is
> for the Candelabrum... and other than that, they're just really crappy
> light sources.  Let's make some better ones.
> 
> -----
> 
> Incense of Meditation:  Found in quantities of 1-2, unidentified as
> 'candles'.  When lit, they make your spell points regenerate as if you
> were a wizard with the Eye of the Aethiopica.  Don't last very long,
> though.
> 
> Incense of Evocation: Same as above.  When lit, all spell damage is
> doubled, and all spells are twice as likely to work or be cast
> successfully. (Make this a -4 to saves for the monsters that get hit
> with spells that don't do damage?  I.E. Sleep, Polymorph, Slow
> Monster, etc.)  Again, doesn't last long.
> 
> And of course, along with those we need incense for those who jump the
> gun and light candles first.  They can't be dropped or extinguished,
> and they start uncursed but auto-curse (like the dunce cap) when
> activated.
> 
> Incense of Enervation:  Same as above.  When lit, they halt all spell
> point regeneration.  These last a LONG time.
> 
> Incense of Draining: Same as above.  When lit, they drain spell points
> with each spell cast (like the AoY does).
> 
I like these candle ideas. It'd be cool to have some non-spell related 
effects too; they could be used to grant temporary intrinsics. Good ones 
could grant resistances (fire, cold, electrical make the most sense), 
regeneration, extra damage, even a temporary bonus to luck. Bad could 
grant aggrivate monster, hunger, or other minuses.

Basically they could be like rings, only temporary.

Adding so many new items to the game is really more of a Slash'EM thing. 
Still, I'd like to see vanilla implement a few of these. Also it should 
get rid of one of the current two types of candles; IIRC the wax is 
basically just a double tallow candle.

So you could have wax candles, and maybe three magic candle types: two 
good, one bad. I suggest one good one regenerates spell points and the 
other regenerates health. The bad one stops all regeneration (or negates 
the regeneration intrinsic, if you have it, leaving you with the base 
regeneration).

